  "lessons": [
    {
      "id": "BN-R01-tumi-again",
      "sequence": 1310,
      "title": "তুমি (tumi), at the far end",
      "headword": "তুমি",
      "romanization": "tumi",
      "gloss": "the familiar you, retrieved a hundred lessons after it was written",
      "script": "bengali",
      "modality": "pen",
      "derivedModality": "pen",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "writing-block"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:98217db4923991e8",
      "notice": {
        "modality": "pen",
        "needs": [],
        "waitUntilStopped": [
          "Writing — from sound"
        ],
        "text": "Before we start: this one needs your hands, so it is not a driving lesson. You can listen to everything else now — leave the section called Writing — from sound until you have stopped, and I will say so again when we reach it."
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 5,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 5s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before anything is uncovered: say you to a friend, you to a stranger, and what."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice — the distant band",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "This chapter has one job, and it is not to teach you anything."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Everything asked for here was first taught between a hundred and a hundred and four lessons ago. That distance is deliberate. A thing recalled after a day is being remembered; a thing recalled after a hundred lessons is being owned, and the only way to find out which you have is to reach that far and see what comes back."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Nothing new arrives in this chapter. If a word does not come, do not treat that as a failure — treat it as the measurement working."
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "you, to a friend — tumi",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *you*, to a friend — *tumi*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "you, to someone you have only now met — āpni",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *you*, to someone you have only now met — *āpni*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "what — ki",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *what* — *ki*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "the whole question, \"what's your name?\" — tomār nām ki?",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: the whole question, \"what's your name?\" — *tomār nām ki?*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "the same question, respectfully — āpnār nām ki?",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: the same question, respectfully — *āpnār nām ki?*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three of those five you have not been asked for in eighty lessons."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "writing",
          "title": "Writing — from sound",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Cover every Bengali model in this book. Write tumi from the sound alone, then write the vowel ই standing on its own."
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "WRITE",
              "instruction": "তুমি (tumi)",
              "spoken": false,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU WRITE: তুমি]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "WRITE",
              "instruction": "ই",
              "spoken": false,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU WRITE: ই]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Which sign in তুমি (tumi) hangs below the line? (ু.) And which \"you\" would you use with a shopkeeper you do not know? (আপনি.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "BN-R01-ta-u-again",
      "sequence": 1320,
      "title": "নাম (nām), and two pieces from the signs chapter",
      "headword": "নাম",
      "romanization": "nām",
      "gloss": "name — and the two pieces of the signs chapter, at their fourth spacing",
      "script": "bengali",
      "modality": "pen",
      "derivedModality": "pen",
      "modalityReasons": [
        "writing-block"
      ],
      "sourceHash": "fnv1a64:eed749607b2a8314",
      "notice": {
        "modality": "pen",
        "needs": [],
        "waitUntilStopped": [
          "Writing — from sound"
        ],
        "text": "Before we start: this one needs your hands, so it is not a driving lesson. You can listen to everything else now — leave the section called Writing — from sound until you have stopped, and I will say so again when we reach it."
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 5,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 5s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say name, then my, then put them together."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice — the distant band",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "name — nām",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *name* — *nām*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "my — āmār",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *my* — *āmār*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "\"my name is —\" with your own name in it",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: \"my name is —\" with your own name in it]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "what Bengali does not put in that sentence (no \"is\")",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: what Bengali does *not* put in that sentence (**no \"is\"**)]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The missing verb is the part that decays first, because English keeps insisting it belongs there. Say the sentence once more without it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "writing",
          "title": "Writing — from sound",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Cover every model. Write the dental consonant, then the sign that hangs beneath a letter, then the word for name."
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "WRITE",
              "instruction": "ত",
              "spoken": false,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU WRITE: ত]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "WRITE",
              "instruction": "ু",
              "spoken": false,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU WRITE: ু]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "WRITE",
              "instruction": "নাম (nām)",
              "spoken": false,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU WRITE: নাম]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Is Bengali's ত made at the teeth or behind them? (At the teeth.) And how many pieces are in নাম (nām)? (Three.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
