      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 5,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 5s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say thank you, and then the thing a Bengali speaker is more likely to say instead of it."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice — the distant band",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "thank you — dhônyobad",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *thank you* — *dhônyobad*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "\"it's no matter / you're welcome\" — kono bæpār nā",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: \"it's no matter / you're welcome\" — *kono bæpār nā*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "what য sounds like standing alone (j)",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: what **য** sounds like standing alone (***j***)]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "what it sounds like hung under another letter (nothing — it bends the vowel to æ)",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: what it sounds like hung under another letter (**nothing** — it bends the vowel to **æ**)]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Both of the words above carry that hung য, and it is the same job in each: the ny in dhônyobad and the byæ in bæpār. Two words from two different chapters, one piece of machinery."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "writing",
          "title": "Writing — from sound",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Cover every model. Write the letter that is written y and said j, then the mark that kills an inherent vowel, then hang the first under a হ."
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "WRITE",
              "instruction": "য",
              "spoken": false,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU WRITE: য]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "WRITE",
              "instruction": "্",
              "spoken": false,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU WRITE: ্]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "WRITE",
              "instruction": "হ্য",
              "spoken": false,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU WRITE: হ্য]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What is the scribes' name for a য hung below? (jô-phôla.) And what does ্ do? (Deletes the inherent vowel.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "BN-R01-chandrabindu-again",
