        "needs": [],
        "waitUntilStopped": [
          "Writing — from sound"
        ],
        "text": "Before we start: this one needs your hands, so it is not a driving lesson. You can listen to everything else now — leave the section called Writing — from sound until you have stopped, and I will say so again when we reach it."
      },
      "blocks": [
        {
          "index": 0,
          "type": "warmup",
          "title": "Warm-up",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 5,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 5s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say yes and no."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice — the distant band",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "yes — hyã, through the nose",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *yes* — *hyã*, through the nose]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "no — nā, not through the nose",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *no* — *nā*, not through the nose]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "the number five — pā̃ch, and notice the same nasal",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: the number five — *pā̃ch*, and notice the same nasal]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "where on the line the mark that writes it sits (above)",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: where on the line the mark that writes it sits (**above**)]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Three words in this whole book carry that crescent, and they are spread across three chapters. That is exactly the shape of thing a reader loses: rare enough to go, common enough to matter."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say hyã and nā one after another until the difference is in the nose and not in the effort."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "writing",
          "title": "Writing — from sound",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Cover every model. Write the crescent-with-a-dot, then put it on না."
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "WRITE",
              "instruction": "ঁ ((chôndrobindu))",
              "spoken": false,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU WRITE: ঁ]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "WRITE",
              "instruction": "নাঁ",
              "spoken": false,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU WRITE: নাঁ]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Is ঁ ((chôndrobindu)) a consonant? (No.) What does it change? (The vowel — it goes through the nose.) And is it the only mark above the head-line? (Yes.)"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
