          "title": "Guided Practice — the distant band",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "hello, and goodbye, with one word — nômoshkar",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: hello, and goodbye, with one word — *nômoshkar*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "yes — hyã",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *yes* — *hyã*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "how many pieces are in each (seven, and five)",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: how many pieces are in each (**seven**, and **five**)]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "These two words are the bookends of the reading strand. The greeting was the first thing you could decode and it took nine lessons of letters to earn. Yes came three chapters later and cost three."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The difference is not that the second word is simpler. It is that by the time it arrived you already owned four of its five pieces — which is the argument for buying letters early and spending them often, made in two words."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "writing",
          "title": "Writing — from sound",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Cover every model. Write yes, then the breath-letter alone, then the last consonant of the greeting."
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "WRITE",
              "instruction": "হ্যাঁ (hyã)",
              "spoken": false,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU WRITE: হ্যাঁ]"
            },
            {
