              "instruction": "\"I am well\" without the pronoun (bhālo āchhi)",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: \"I am well\" **without** the pronoun (*bhālo āchhi*)]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "That last one is the test. The pronoun is carried by the ি on the end of the verb, so a speaker who drops আমি (āmi) loses nothing at all — and a learner who cannot drop it is still translating rather than speaking."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Say the polite formula once more, whole, at speed. It is the longest thing this book asks anyone to say from memory."
            }
